Package: Rveg
Title: Digitization of Phytosociological Relevés
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R: c( 
    person("Přemysl", "Král", , "kralp@fzp.czu.cz", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2887-651X")),
    person("Jan", "Douda", , "douda@fzp.czu.cz", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1205-364X")))
Description: Digitizes, manages, and classifies phytosociological vegetation
    plots. Includes a checklist of Czech vascular plants based on
    Danihelka, Chrtek, and Kaplan (2012)
    <https://www.preslia.cz/article/159>. Imports vegetation data from
    'TURBOVEG' (Hennekens and Schaminée, 2001)
    <doi:10.2307/3237010> and exports data for 'JUICE' (Tichý, 2002)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1654-1103.2002.tb02069.x>. Supports vegetation
    classification using 'CzechVeg-ESy' expert rules (Chytrý et al., 2020)
    <doi:10.5281/zenodo.3605562> and a constancy-based classifier inspired
    by 'VegKey' (Tichý and Chytrý, 2019) <doi:10.1111/jvs.12799>.
    The bundled default classification model was trained on
    'CzechVeg-OpenStrat' (Chytrý et al., 2026)
    <doi:10.5281/zenodo.19231152>. Resolves plant synonyms using the
    World Checklist of Vascular Plants (Govaerts et al., 2021)
    <doi:10.1038/s41597-021-00997-6>, the taxonomic backbone of
    'Plants of the World Online'. For package methodology, see
    Král and Douda (2025) <doi:10.1111/jvs.70012>.
URL: https://plant-ecology-lab-czu.com/resources/rveg/,
    https://github.com/sesitcsl2/Rveg
